WEBVTT

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:52.278
What number are you?

00:01:55.073 --> 00:01:56.366
Do you want to go home?

00:01:59.744 --> 00:02:02.872
Kazuya Tokugawa, Court 1.

00:02:16.094 --> 00:02:22.100
"The Gatekeeper of Hell"

00:02:25.562 --> 00:02:26.855
Sheesh.

00:02:26.855 --> 00:02:30.233
I can't believe he made me lug
this all the way out here.

00:02:30.233 --> 00:02:33.820
Echizen's a real slave driver!

00:02:35.155 --> 00:02:37.782
I finally made it.

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:40.285
Wait...

00:02:44.539 --> 00:02:48.752
Wha-- What is this, a prison?!

00:02:59.888 --> 00:03:01.431
This is amazing.

00:03:01.431 --> 00:03:03.641
It's like a high end hotel.

00:03:03.641 --> 00:03:06.478
Hey, can we eat all of this?

00:03:06.478 --> 00:03:10.440
Yes. Please eat all you like,
of whatever you'd like.

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:12.067
Yahoo!

00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:13.985
Hey, morons...

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:17.989
Don't you think you're getting too excited?

00:03:19.741 --> 00:03:20.867
What'd you say?

00:03:21.159 --> 00:03:23.411
If you're going to treat
this like a field trip,

00:03:23.411 --> 00:03:26.581
pack your bags and get out of here.

00:03:26.581 --> 00:03:27.791
You're an eyesore.

00:03:30.794 --> 00:03:33.463
Calm down, Viper.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:36.508
But we've got delicious food,

00:03:36.508 --> 00:03:40.261
the latest training machines,
and even hot springs.

00:03:40.261 --> 00:03:43.264
This camp might be more fun than I thought.

00:03:43.264 --> 00:03:44.099
Yeah...

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:57.320
Today's shuffle matches have been announced!

00:04:01.533 --> 00:04:04.119
Look. Your name's up there, Momo.

00:04:04.119 --> 00:04:05.745
"Jujiroh Oni (Court 5) VS
Takeshi Momoshiro (Middle Schooler)"
You're right.

00:04:05.745 --> 00:04:07.664
"Jujiroh Oni (Court 5) VS
Takeshi Momoshiro (Middle Schooler)"
Yahoo, lucky!

00:04:07.664 --> 00:04:08.039
Yahoo, lucky!

00:04:08.039 --> 00:04:11.710
A match already! I'm psyched!

00:04:11.710 --> 00:04:16.006
Momo's the only middle
schooler who was selected.

00:04:16.548 --> 00:04:20.677
And he's playing against
Court 5's Jujiroh Oni.

00:04:24.723 --> 00:04:27.308
It should be an interesting match.

00:04:45.493 --> 00:04:47.954
What's with his racquet?

00:04:47.954 --> 00:04:50.248
It's only got two strings.

00:04:51.207 --> 00:04:54.794
He can't possibly mean to play with that.

00:04:56.254 --> 00:05:00.008
You've got quite the open racquet there.

00:05:02.427 --> 00:05:06.056
Seishun Academy second
year, Takeshi Momoshiro.

00:05:06.056 --> 00:05:10.018
If I win this shuffle
match, I'll be in Court 5.

00:05:15.148 --> 00:05:15.982
Impossible.

00:05:42.175 --> 00:05:43.760
You can do it, Momo!

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:46.930
Show that high schooler who's boss!

00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:50.266
Hey, now. It's time to start
taking this seriously.

00:05:50.558 --> 00:05:55.146
You guys don't know anything about Oni-<i>san</i>.

00:05:55.939 --> 00:06:00.068
What sort of player is this Oni guy?

00:06:00.527 --> 00:06:03.488
Court 5, Jujiroh Oni.

00:06:03.905 --> 00:06:07.492
Nicknamed the "Gatekeeper of Hell,"

00:06:07.492 --> 00:06:09.744
for crushing those who rise to his court.

00:06:10.245 --> 00:06:11.830
The Gatekeeper of Hell?

00:06:12.288 --> 00:06:13.915
That's hardly genial.

00:06:14.791 --> 00:06:19.838
Apparently, he is strong enough
to lift one ton boulders.

00:06:20.630 --> 00:06:24.509
Which makes this a match
between two power players.

00:06:27.887 --> 00:06:29.597
Well, then...

00:06:29.597 --> 00:06:33.059
Time to slay me an Oni!

00:06:36.688 --> 00:06:40.692
Let's see what Court 5 can do.

00:06:41.192 --> 00:06:42.485
Too slow!

00:06:45.405 --> 00:06:46.239
Impossible.

00:06:46.656 --> 00:06:51.578
He returned Momoshiro's heavyweight
serve with a two-stringed racquet.

00:06:51.578 --> 00:06:53.621
You'll have to do better than that!

00:06:55.498 --> 00:06:57.292
I'm not surprised.

00:06:57.292 --> 00:06:59.336
He's nothing like the other high schoolers.

00:07:00.712 --> 00:07:02.380
I can't underestimate him!

00:07:02.797 --> 00:07:03.798
A feint!

00:07:03.798 --> 00:07:04.632
Impressive!

00:07:05.175 --> 00:07:06.676
Come at me!

00:07:09.429 --> 00:07:10.930
That's it.

00:07:11.348 --> 00:07:13.475
Send him home packing!

00:07:14.642 --> 00:07:16.686
Give him your specialty!

00:07:20.482 --> 00:07:25.320
Don't underestimate us middle schoolers!

00:07:25.612 --> 00:07:28.281
There it is! Momoshiro's Jack Knife!

00:07:31.159 --> 00:07:32.369
What?

00:07:34.412 --> 00:07:39.000
What do you expect to cut
with that puny little knife?

00:07:39.709 --> 00:07:43.922
I'll show you a real Jack Knife.

00:07:44.964 --> 00:07:47.258
Black Jack Knife!

00:08:09.322 --> 00:08:12.575
Both your wrists are completely shot.

00:08:13.451 --> 00:08:15.995
You won't be able to use them for a while.

00:08:20.917 --> 00:08:22.252
Momo-<i>senpai</i>.

00:08:27.090 --> 00:08:28.758
That's game.

00:08:31.803 --> 00:08:33.513
That's our Oni-<i>san</i>.

00:08:33.888 --> 00:08:35.640
That was quick.

00:08:42.313 --> 00:08:43.982
Where are you going?

00:08:44.524 --> 00:08:46.776
This match isn't over yet.

00:08:56.036 --> 00:08:58.913
I've still got a lot of fight left in me.

00:09:05.045 --> 00:09:08.048
Echizen's not answering.

00:09:08.631 --> 00:09:12.927
How am I supposed to bring him
his stuff if I can't get inside?

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:15.430
Hey, you!

00:09:16.348 --> 00:09:18.391
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:09:18.391 --> 00:09:21.227
I promise I've got a good reason to be here!

00:09:21.227 --> 00:09:22.937
I'm not up to anything shady!

00:09:23.396 --> 00:09:24.272
Huh?

00:09:25.315 --> 00:09:27.776
What's this? Aren't you...

00:09:27.776 --> 00:09:30.820
Yamabuki Middle School
first year, Taichi Dan.

00:09:30.820 --> 00:09:35.116
I came to deliver the charm
Akutsu-<i>senpai </i>forgot.

00:09:35.116 --> 00:09:36.701
Dan-<i>san</i>!

00:09:36.951 --> 00:09:38.620
Dan-<i>san</i>, Dan-<i>san</i>.

00:09:38.995 --> 00:09:41.539
I found a hole that should take us inside.

00:09:41.790 --> 00:09:43.124
Really?

00:09:43.124 --> 00:09:45.126
Let's check it out.

00:09:45.752 --> 00:09:46.461
Oh...

00:09:47.128 --> 00:09:50.382
This is Rikkai first year Shiita Urayama-<i>kun</i>.

00:09:50.382 --> 00:09:51.883
I ran into him here.

00:09:52.300 --> 00:09:55.470
This is Horio-<i>kun</i>, one of the
Seigaku Cheerleading Trio...

00:09:55.470 --> 00:09:58.348
Hey! Who are you calling a cheerleader?!

00:10:03.603 --> 00:10:05.313
Ow.

00:10:06.439 --> 00:10:08.983
His shots are so strong.

00:10:10.151 --> 00:10:11.319
Fool.

00:10:12.362 --> 00:10:15.740
What can you do with those ruined wrists?

00:10:29.170 --> 00:10:31.006
Come on, bring it!

00:10:35.301 --> 00:10:38.888
How long is Momoshiro gonna keep this up?

00:10:41.099 --> 00:10:44.227
He can't win if he can't hold his racquet.

00:10:52.027 --> 00:10:53.653
Stop, Momo!

00:10:53.653 --> 00:10:57.323
If you keep going, you could
cause irreparable damage!

00:10:57.824 --> 00:11:02.078
Did you forget our promise to make
it through this camp together?

00:11:03.079 --> 00:11:04.414
Sorry, Senpai.

00:11:05.749 --> 00:11:08.877
I can't lose now.

00:11:11.880 --> 00:11:13.590
Guts and fight.

00:11:15.759 --> 00:11:19.137
Hell's full of kids like you.

00:11:19.888 --> 00:11:21.681
Black Jack Knife!

00:11:21.681 --> 00:11:23.641
Watch out, Momoshiro!

00:11:30.106 --> 00:11:32.859
Stop, Momo! You've got to forfeit!

00:11:32.859 --> 00:11:36.321
Even if you don't win this match,
you can try again next time!

00:11:37.072 --> 00:11:38.406
Did you hear that?

00:11:38.823 --> 00:11:40.533
Even your friends agree.

00:11:41.159 --> 00:11:43.703
Why don't you just give up?

00:11:45.330 --> 00:11:46.748
Sorry, but...

00:11:47.624 --> 00:11:53.421
I've always been a bad kid who
doesn't listen to his seniors.

00:11:55.090 --> 00:12:00.345
The real Oni hunt has only just begun.

00:12:01.346 --> 00:12:02.555
This kid...

00:12:11.773 --> 00:12:13.858
Where are we?

00:12:14.693 --> 00:12:17.737
We seem to be inside.

00:12:18.321 --> 00:12:21.658
Huh? That's Momo-<i>chan</i>-<i>senpai</i>.

00:12:21.991 --> 00:12:24.160
Hey, Momo-<i>chan</i>-<i>senpa</i>--

00:12:26.788 --> 00:12:28.873
He's all beat up.

00:12:28.873 --> 00:12:32.252
What sort of training is he doing?

00:12:33.545 --> 00:12:35.797
If you want to go to Hell, then go!

00:12:35.797 --> 00:12:38.174
I'll even send you off
with a nice parting gift!

00:12:38.758 --> 00:12:40.552
Don't hold back!

00:12:40.552 --> 00:12:42.595
Hit me with your best shot!

00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:45.181
How unlucky.

00:12:46.099 --> 00:12:50.437
The Jack Knife user Momoshiro has
the bad luck to face off against

00:12:50.437 --> 00:12:55.483
the user of a more than twice as
powerful and precise Jack Knife.

00:12:55.942 --> 00:12:58.361
No, it might not be luck.

00:13:00.488 --> 00:13:03.658
If the coaches planned this...

00:13:05.493 --> 00:13:06.953
I knew it.

00:13:07.454 --> 00:13:13.877
If their plan is to shut us middle
schoolers up, it might be working.

00:13:14.294 --> 00:13:19.174
Yeah, but Momoshiro's a different story.

00:13:22.385 --> 00:13:24.095
Arrogant bastard!

00:13:24.596 --> 00:13:25.930
He can still hold it?

00:13:26.389 --> 00:13:28.183
If I lose...

00:13:28.600 --> 00:13:31.353
If I lose here...

00:13:31.686 --> 00:13:37.025
they'll never take any of the
middle schoolers here seriously!

00:13:38.985 --> 00:13:40.320
Momoshiro!

00:13:42.405 --> 00:13:43.198
Momo!

00:13:43.907 --> 00:13:45.158
One hit is enough...

00:13:45.492 --> 00:13:47.035
Just one hit!

00:13:48.995 --> 00:13:50.330
Momo-<i>senpai</i>...

00:13:57.087 --> 00:13:59.255
Black Jack Knife!

00:14:07.514 --> 00:14:09.265
Game and match, Oni.

00:14:09.265 --> 00:14:10.725
Six games to love.

00:14:14.604 --> 00:14:19.025
Thank... you... Oni-<i>senpai</i>.

00:14:25.323 --> 00:14:29.244
He broke my strings with
that last Jack Knife.

00:14:35.417 --> 00:14:36.584
This kid...

00:14:37.711 --> 00:14:41.089
What's your name again?

00:14:42.716 --> 00:14:45.844
Takeshi... Momoshiro.

00:14:51.141 --> 00:14:54.978
Work your way up, Takeshi Momoshiro!

00:15:03.778 --> 00:15:05.113
Mo-Momo!

00:15:05.113 --> 00:15:06.114
Are you okay?

00:15:06.114 --> 00:15:07.407
Talk about sad.

00:15:08.658 --> 00:15:13.038
Well, this is all middle schoolers can do.

00:15:13.038 --> 00:15:18.293
They're years away from standing a
chance against us high schoolers.

00:15:21.671 --> 00:15:28.178
Hey, the strongest one among you
guys is that Tokugawa, right?

00:15:43.860 --> 00:15:48.281
A capybara lost in a pride of lions.

00:15:48.907 --> 00:15:51.701
The gap between the upper court

00:15:51.701 --> 00:15:55.455
high schoolers and the middle
schoolers is obvious.

00:15:56.289 --> 00:16:00.460
You could say there is nothing they can do.

00:16:01.670 --> 00:16:06.341
However, the capybara will
sometimes attack the lions.

00:16:07.509 --> 00:16:12.013
Nothing is more unpredictable than a
weak animal when it's cornered.

00:16:13.932 --> 00:16:16.768
I believe today's training is...

00:16:19.145 --> 00:16:22.732
I hope they can handle it.

00:16:28.863 --> 00:16:33.201
I'm glad none of your bones were broken.

00:16:33.493 --> 00:16:35.912
You shouldn't scare us like that.

00:16:35.912 --> 00:16:38.373
Sorry for making you worry.

00:16:39.040 --> 00:16:44.504
You don't think about the
consequences enough, you moron.

00:16:44.504 --> 00:16:46.297
What'd you say?!

00:16:46.297 --> 00:16:47.882
You wanna fight?

00:16:49.342 --> 00:16:52.303
If you've got that much
energy, you should be fine.

00:16:52.804 --> 00:16:55.223
But you can't get complacent just yet.

00:16:55.557 --> 00:17:00.478
You should avoid holding your racquet
until the numbness goes away.

00:17:00.478 --> 00:17:02.647
Got it.

00:17:03.314 --> 00:17:07.777
Looks like we'll have to
watch out for these coaches.

00:17:07.777 --> 00:17:08.528
Yes,

00:17:09.029 --> 00:17:13.491
but for us, who have endured
Rikkai's harsh training,

00:17:13.491 --> 00:17:15.368
there's nothing to be afraid of.

00:17:15.827 --> 00:17:19.539
We'll just have to wait and see.

00:17:20.749 --> 00:17:22.751
Sounds interesting.

00:17:22.751 --> 00:17:25.295
How are they gonna play with us next?

00:17:26.463 --> 00:17:28.715
What should we do?

00:17:28.715 --> 00:17:31.843
I'm gonna watch them practice some more.

00:17:31.843 --> 00:17:34.763
I've gotta get this stuff to Echizen.

00:17:34.763 --> 00:17:36.973
Hey, middle schoolers...

00:17:39.684 --> 00:17:41.853
--Ow...
--Who is that?

00:17:42.854 --> 00:17:44.814
He's huge!

00:17:44.814 --> 00:17:48.068
About 2.16 meters.

00:17:49.486 --> 00:17:53.198
He must be a real klutz
to hit his head on that.

00:17:53.948 --> 00:17:55.784
Good morning, everyone.

00:17:55.784 --> 00:17:58.244
I'm your U-17 Mental Coach...

00:17:58.578 --> 00:18:00.663
...Saitoh!

00:18:00.663 --> 00:18:01.998
Coach?

00:18:02.582 --> 00:18:06.044
I've been observing your matches.

00:18:06.378 --> 00:18:10.048
You're all much stronger than I
would expect of middle schoolers.

00:18:11.049 --> 00:18:16.971
But strengthening your mental
ability will make you even better.

00:18:18.682 --> 00:18:19.974
Mental ability.

00:18:21.017 --> 00:18:23.895
First, pair up.

00:18:23.895 --> 00:18:25.647
Anyone's fine.

00:18:26.356 --> 00:18:30.777
Pairs! Oishi, we're finally
gonna get to play doubles!

00:18:30.777 --> 00:18:32.487
Let's do this!

00:18:33.405 --> 00:18:34.614
Oh, my.

00:18:41.454 --> 00:18:42.539
Let's join up.

00:18:43.665 --> 00:18:46.793
Want to work together
like we used to, Yuta?

00:18:47.168 --> 00:18:48.753
Hey, Hiroshi.

00:18:49.796 --> 00:18:51.631
I'll pair up with you.

00:18:52.090 --> 00:18:55.093
I, the captain of the Hyotei Academy team,

00:18:55.093 --> 00:18:57.178
will instruct you personally.

00:18:57.595 --> 00:19:01.057
C-Captain, would you group up with me?

00:19:01.808 --> 00:19:03.018
Very well.

00:19:03.893 --> 00:19:05.311
Thank you.

00:19:05.937 --> 00:19:11.568
Oh, crap. Pairs are already
forming everywhere.

00:19:12.193 --> 00:19:16.197
Who hasn't paired up yet?

00:19:25.957 --> 00:19:27.042
Huh?

00:19:27.709 --> 00:19:30.795
The location of Court 1 isn't on here.

00:19:31.296 --> 00:19:33.048
Hey, middle schooler.

00:19:34.049 --> 00:19:35.508
What are you doing?

00:19:35.759 --> 00:19:38.845
Practice should have started already.

00:19:38.845 --> 00:19:42.057
Hey, I'm looking for Court 1.

00:19:42.057 --> 00:19:43.725
Could you tell me where it is?

00:19:44.976 --> 00:19:46.311
What?

00:19:48.104 --> 00:19:51.524
Huh? Where am I?

00:19:51.524 --> 00:19:54.569
I got lost looking for the bathroom.

00:19:55.236 --> 00:19:56.237
Hey!

00:19:56.237 --> 00:19:58.990
That's Koshimae!

00:19:59.282 --> 00:20:02.494
Court 1... Why do you want to know?

00:20:02.869 --> 00:20:05.372
It's got nothing to do with you.

00:20:05.747 --> 00:20:07.415
Just tell me.

00:20:09.959 --> 00:20:15.006
We'll tell you, but only after you beat us.

00:20:16.466 --> 00:20:19.260
Hey, Koshimae!

00:20:19.678 --> 00:20:22.180
You doing something fun?

00:20:23.264 --> 00:20:25.684
Let me join!

00:20:27.310 --> 00:20:28.895
Did you form your pairs?

00:20:33.441 --> 00:20:35.026
You will now play

00:20:35.026 --> 00:20:37.862
singles matches.

00:20:37.862 --> 00:20:39.948
What? Singles?

00:20:39.948 --> 00:20:41.658
We're not playing doubles?

00:20:42.450 --> 00:20:45.370
Those who lose will drop out.

00:20:46.079 --> 00:20:50.333
You will play against the partners
you just paired up with.

00:20:53.712 --> 00:20:56.089
The losers drop out?!

00:20:56.089 --> 00:20:59.217
They have to defeat each
other by friendly fire!

00:20:59.551 --> 00:21:03.013
Oh, no! This is terrible!

00:21:09.853 --> 00:21:11.354
Yahoo!

00:21:12.647 --> 00:21:15.233
Doubles with Koshimae!

00:21:15.233 --> 00:21:17.027
Let's go!

00:21:18.778 --> 00:21:21.573
What cocky middle schoolers.

00:21:22.323 --> 00:21:24.743
We'll have to fix that.

00:21:26.369 --> 00:21:27.370
Ready?

00:21:27.912 --> 00:21:28.747
Let's go.

00:21:33.710 --> 00:21:34.669
What?

00:21:37.005 --> 00:21:39.090
Th-This kid...

00:23:17.063 --> 00:23:18.481
"Preview"

00:23:18.481 --> 00:23:20.525
"Preview"
Whoops! I messed up again!

00:23:20.525 --> 00:23:21.276
Whoops! I messed up again!

00:23:22.068 --> 00:23:22.986
Eiji!

00:23:22.986 --> 00:23:27.699
I'm getting to play with Oishi,
but nothing's going right.

00:23:27.699 --> 00:23:31.828
Enough, Eiji. What good will that do?

00:23:32.537 --> 00:23:35.123
What should I do, then?

00:23:35.123 --> 00:23:37.292
The loser has to drop out!

00:23:40.795 --> 00:23:42.797
"Friendly Fire"
The next episode of <i>Prince</i>
<i>of Tennis II </i>is: "Friendly Fire."

00:23:42.797 --> 00:23:44.424
"Friendly Fire"
I won't lose to you.

00:23:44.424 --> 00:23:47.094
"Friendly Fire"
I'll win and continue my stay at this camp.
